{"timestamp":"2026-11-10T06:27:16.209Z","ordinal":146,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1c41e-f65a-74d1-89e8-e216ba74503e","turn_id":"01a1c423-44ef-7eb3-80be-32a675401ba4","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_096428d272974f1a016af2b9401ad887d092278c28001c3b26","content":[{"type":"Text","text":":codex-annotation{index=\"1\"} Fairly straightforward. I’ve inspected the code but haven’t edited it.\n\nI’d make three changes:\n\n1. **Shared grouping:** Group edit snapshots by session and turn for both `sun log` and `sun viz`. Each turn becomes one row, with individual calls and patches retained in its details.\n2. **Subagent tracking:** Initialize turn state when a subagent first calls a tool, so new edits don’t become `turn0`.\n3. **Regression tests:** Cover interleaved agents, already-squashed turns, and subagents.\n\nThe main wrinkle is old `turn0` records: we can’t safely assume they all belong to one turn. I’d leave those separate unless transcript evidence establishes their boundaries.\n\nThis is a modest display and bookkeeping change. It doesn’t require rewriting existing Git history."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1794292032064,"completed_at_ms":1794292036209}}
